To further improve the weighted rating of this implementation, we can optimize the `convertIncomingMessageToIntermediateFormat` method by minimizing the number of intermediate messages being created. Currently, for each incoming message, we apply all incoming message converters and merge their results using `mergeAll`. This can result in unnecessary overhead and memory usage, especially for high message volumes.

One possible solution is to introduce a priority system among the converters and execute them in order of priority. The converter with highest priority will be executed first, followed by others with lower priorities. If any converter returns a non-null value, we stop executing the remaining converters and pass the converted result upstream. This way, we avoid creating multiple intermediate messages for a single incoming message.

Here's an updated implementation that introduces a priority system:

```typescript
private convertIncomingMessageToIntermediateFormat() {
  return pipe(
    mergeMap((original) =>
      this.getHighestPriorityConverter().pipe(
        switchMap((converter) =>
          converter.convert(original).pipe(
            tap((result) => {
              if (result) {
                this.runDecisionTreeHandlers(result);
              }
            })
          )
        ),
        catchError(() => of(undefined)),
        mergeMap((converted) =>
          this.getNextLowerPriorityConverters(converter).pipe(
            mergeMap((lowerPriorityConverter) =>
              lowerPriorityConverter.convert(original).pipe(
                tap((result) => {
                  if (result) {
                    this.runDecisionTreeHandlers(result);
                  }
                })
              )
            )
          )
        )
      )
    ),
    mergeAll()
  );
}

private getHighestPriorityConverter() {
  // Return the converter with highest priority
  return this.incomingMessageConverters[0];
}

private getNextLowerPriorityConverters(currentConverter: UwpTextDataBus.IIncomingMessageConverter) {
  const index = this.incomingMessageConverters.findIndex(
    (converter) => converter !== currentConverter && converter.priority <= currentConverter.priority
  );

