To create a socket for chatroom in PHP, you can use the built-in stream sockets library provided by PHP. Here's an example of how to set up a basic WebSocket server using this library:

First, let's define our WebSocket handler function that will handle incoming connections and messages:

```php
function onWebSocketConnect($resource) {
    // Get the remote IP address and port number of the connecting client
    list($remoteAddress, $remotePort) = stream_socket_client(sprintf("tcp://127.0.0.1:%d", rand(1024, 65535)), 30, STREAM_CLIENT_CONNECT | STREAM_CLIENT_PERSISTENT);

    // Save the resource ID and IP address of the connecting client
    $clients[] = array(
        "socket" => $resource,
        "address" => $remoteAddress
    );

    // Send a welcome message back to the client
    socket_write($resource, "Welcome! ", 13);
    return true;
}

function onWebSocketMessage($resource, $data) {
    foreach ($clients as $client) {
        // Check if the message was intended for this client
        if (substr($data, 0, strlen($client["address"])) === $client["address"]) {
            // If so, send it back to the client
            socket_write($client["socket"], $data, strlen($data));
            return true;
        }
    }

    // If not, broadcast the message to all clients
    foreach ($clients as $client) {
        socket_write($client["socket"], $data, strlen($data));
    }
    return true;
}

function onWebSocketClose($code, $resource) {
    foreach ($clients as $key => $client) {
        if ($client["socket"] === $resource) {
            unset($clients[$key]);
            break;
        }
    }
    return true;
}

function onWebSocketError($errno, $errstr, $resource) {
    return true;
}
```

